# Screw mate (an extension): with nothing fitting selected, it says what
# to select; the top circles of the holes of two linked plates, the
# second active, made a screw mate: the second plate goes on the first's
# axis, turned by the new parameter turn and moved along it by lead, the
# M4's coarse pitch, per turn. Then turn is set to 90 in the parameter
# table, and the plate turns a quarter and rises a quarter of the lead.
file $testdata/ui/screw_pair.tlspr
menu File|Open...
key f
answer ok
menu Assembly|Mate Screw
move 245 185
down L 245 185
up L 245 185
move 445 195
down L 445 195
up L 445 195
menu Assembly|Mate Screw
tw
twmove 60 255
twdown L 60 255
twup L 60 255
tw
twmove 420 115
twdown L 420 115
twup L 420 115
edit 90
tw
save
